  "query_preview": "..Temperatures 5 to 10 degrees above average again\ntoday with light winds before some changes begin to move into the\narea starting Saturday. A west coast trough begins to move towards\nthe area which will start a cooling trend, but more noteworthy\nchange is the uptick in the winds. Any moisture associated with\nthis troughs stays well to the north so the air mass will remain\non the dry side, which along with the elevated winds will lead to\nmultiple days of near critical to critical fire weather concerns.\nA Red Flag Warning is in effect Saturday for our northwestern\nzones, with a Fire Weather Watch in effect Sunday for a good\nportion of Northern Arizona.  \n\nThe trough will be a slow moving one and will keep our\ntemperatures near average for most of next week. It will also\nkeep the dry air mass over us and with continued elevated winds\neach afternoon, fire weather will continue to be a concern over\nmost of the week with more headlines likely being issued as the\nweek progresses.",
